            <ArticleTitle>Late onset painful cold-aggravated myotonia: three families with SCN4A L1436P mutation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>590-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.nmd.2011.05.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe three Belgian families with a L1436P mutation in the SCN4A gene, causing a sodium channel myotonia with an atypical clinical presentation, characterized by late onset painful cold-aggravated myotonia. These families represent a distinct phenotype within the spectrum of sodium channel myotonia.</AbstractText>
